{
  "about": "Every predicate field is typed before any record is read (P9, #4854): a comparison whose operand types cannot be compared (FORMULA-5) is refused by check() as by a build, with the same complete issue row, over an input with no record and, for the root and row filters, over one with records. Each case is one field: an assertion's require and when, a row_count filter and a not_missing when, typed by the output columns' declared types; the root filter, typed by the base driver's fields; a row template's filter, typed by its reads; a window filter; a structured source filter, over another input and over the driver; and an aggregate filter, in a column and in a grouped row. Each row is the phase, condition and rule the registry gives incompatible_input_type for a predicate (validation, FORMULA-5), the field's path, and the context of an incomparable pair: left_type and right_type as the comparison writes its operands (a str column against an int literal, or an int field against a str literal), with actual the right operand's type, and an empty operand route. A comparison whose str operand is a field no declaration types and its input may or may not store is left to build, which reads the input's header before any record: stored, the field is str (INPUT-5) and the comparison fails with a hint naming its undeclared type; absent, it is an unknown field. Only the records decide which, so check leaves it (D195, D199), and the root filter's pair of cases states each operation's rows.",
  "documents": {
    "spec": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: ADX\nbase: D\nkeys: [ID]\ninput:\n  D: {path: d.csv, types: {X: int}}\n  E: {path: d.csv, key: [ID], types: {X: int}}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, X]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: D.ID}\n  - {name: X, type: int, derivation: D.X}\n"
  },
  "cases": [
